  "description": "A drive that was never closed gets its terrain elevation once it is closed by hand, long after, also across a restart (requirement 3 of #5940). Without streaming, the car drives north from where it is parked (no terrain data) through B, C and D, where the terrain lies at 100, 130 and 110 m, to E (no terrain data). At B, C and D the lookups at insert cannot answer (the summary's and the recorded position's, two each), so the drive's positions are stored without elevation. Nine vehicle_not_found errors melt the not_found fuse and the vehicle is killed mid-drive, as in a crash; the restarted vehicle knows nothing of the drive, which stays open. Eleven days later on the replay clock, outside the 10-day window of the elevation repair, the drive is closed by hand through Log.close_drive/1, as the documented rpc line does: with no elevations its ascent and descent are 0, and it is queued for Terrain. A first repair pass finds the terrain unable to answer at B, its first position (one more unavailable lookup), and ends; a second pass with a fresh Terrain and repair, as after a restart, fills the queued drive. The restarted vehicle then goes online parked further north and falls asleep; the asleep terminal from :online routes through :start, so the asleep row is the convergence point after the barrier. Pin: the drive's positions at B, C and D get 100, 130 and 110, E keeps none, and the drive's ascent is 30 and its descent 20; the parked positions keep no elevation.",
